  "title": "County worker vacancies and HR consultant review",
  "summary": "On October 8, a commissioner said urgent work lies ahead on vacancies, recruitment, retention and HR reform, after the acting director said turnover is higher than usual and the county does not do enough exit interviews. A consultant's review of recruitment, hiring, classification and reorganization is under way. In July the county had 962 open positions, but departments had sent only 335 requests to fill them.",
